## 1. Cut

Follow the cutting list below and the diagrams in `sheets/`. With a plunge saw: lay each sheet on rigid foam insulation so both sides of every cut are supported, use about 2.6m of joined track for the full-length rips and 213cm crosscuts, and tape the cut lines or score first to stop splintering.
⚠️ The layout assumes a {{ (kerf * 10)|size }}mm saw cut: check your blade's width and rebuild if it's wider.

Each sheet is trimmed {{ edge_trim|size }}cm on every edge, leaving {% for m in usable %}{{ m.length|size }} × {{ m.width|size }}cm of {{ m.material }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}. Rip the strips across the sheet in order with the plunge saw, then crosscut each strip: on the mitre saw for strips up to {{ mitre_capacity|size }}cm wide, with the strip's length supported level with the saw's table, and with the plunge saw for wider ones (marked). Every part's length runs along the grain. Saw cut {{ kerf|size }}cm.
